<title>FRANCE: SOCCER-BRAZIL-ENGLAND GAME SWITCHED TO PARIS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZIL-ENGLAND GAME SWITCHED TO PARIS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazil-England match in a four-nation tournament in France in June has been switched from Lens to the Parc des Princes in Paris.</p>
<p>A Paris spokesman said on Friday that the game, originally scheduled for the Felix Bollaert stadium on June 10, had to be moved after bad weather delayed renovation work on the stadium for the 1998 World Cup.</p>
<p>The Parc des Princes will also stage the match between France and Italy the following day.</p>
</text>
